WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.620 --> 00:00:01.940
Ah Houston?

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:03.580
We got a box office bomb here…

00:00:04.310 --> 00:00:08.580
By all accounts, First Man is an excellent
film, filled with great performances from

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:11.120
stars like Ryan Gosling and Claire Foy.

00:00:11.380 --> 00:00:13.360
So why isn't anyone going to see it?

00:00:13.500 --> 00:00:17.040
Here's a look at why First Man has bombed
at the box office so far.

00:00:17.720 --> 00:00:19.820
On paper, First Man should be a hit.

00:00:20.130 --> 00:00:24.960
Ryan Gosling excels with another masterful
performance as Neil Armstrong, the first man

00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:29.619
to walk on the moon, while rising star Claire
Foy has been earning accolades portraying

00:00:29.620 --> 00:00:30.560
Armstrong's wife.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:34.690
And the talent behind the camera is just as
impressive as the talent in front of it.

00:00:34.690 --> 00:00:38.720
Damien Chazelle won the Best Director Oscar
for La La Land, and he's brought with him

00:00:38.720 --> 00:00:42.840
Oscar-winning La La Land composer Justin Hurwitz
to provide the music.

00:00:42.980 --> 00:00:46.800
And it's all based on an acclaimed biography
about the man at the center of one of the

00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:49.570
greatest accomplishments in human history.

00:00:49.570 --> 00:00:51.460
So why is it underperforming at the box office?

00:00:52.240 --> 00:00:57.040
As the only major release of the weekend of
October 12th, First Man should have had smooth

00:00:57.040 --> 00:00:57.540
sailing.

00:00:57.780 --> 00:01:02.380
Instead, it got caught up in a crazy whirlwind
thanks to the battle between two holdover

00:01:02.390 --> 00:01:06.570
releases from the previous week: A Star Is
Born and Venom.

00:01:06.570 --> 00:01:10.710
Despite bad reviews, Venom managed to claw
its way to the top of the box office two weeks

00:01:10.710 --> 00:01:15.080
in a row, but it was locked in a death struggle
the whole way with the acclaimed remake A

00:01:15.080 --> 00:01:15.980
Star Is Born.

00:01:16.220 --> 00:01:20.640
Between the flash of Lady Gaga's star power
and the over-the-top craziness of Tom Hardy's

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:26.150
alien anti-hero, Ryan Gosling's understated
quietude was drowned out in the noise — leaving

00:01:26.150 --> 00:01:27.840
First Man the odd man out.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:29.360
"Outstanding!

00:01:29.820 --> 00:01:32.220
Now let’s bite all their heads off and pile
them up in the corner.

00:01:32.220 --> 00:01:33.120
"
"why would we do that?"

00:01:33.540 --> 00:01:37.960
The good news for First Man is that critically
acclaimed adult dramas often have long legs

00:01:37.960 --> 00:01:40.940
compared to front-heavy superhero fare like
Venom.

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:45.890
Unfortunately for First Man, though, even
if Venom burns itself out at the box office,

00:01:45.890 --> 00:01:49.960
there's another film waiting in the wings
to claim the box office crown: Halloween.

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:54.660
Earning a stellar $10 million from Thursday
night previews alone, Halloween is on pace

00:01:54.660 --> 00:01:57.900
for an estimated $70 million opening weekend.

00:01:58.229 --> 00:02:03.100
That's on pace to easily win the weekend and
likely bury First Man even further down the

00:02:03.100 --> 00:02:04.000
depth chart.

00:02:04.340 --> 00:02:09.091
When shiny new hits are dominating the conversation
every week, it's hard to generate buzz, even

00:02:09.100 --> 00:02:10.200
if you're Buzz Aldrin.

00:02:10.540 --> 00:02:15.400
First Man has already made back more than
half of its estimated $59 million budget,

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:19.960
so even if it hasn't been a huge hit so far,
it didn't exactly crash and burn, right?

00:02:20.220 --> 00:02:21.360
Well, not so fast.

00:02:21.560 --> 00:02:26.040
Because that figure doesn't take into account
one of the film's biggest costs: marketing.

00:02:26.200 --> 00:02:30.240
While there's no way to know how much money
Universal has spent trying to get butts into

00:02:30.250 --> 00:02:34.470
seats, typically advertising costs run about
half the cost of the film's budget.

00:02:34.470 --> 00:02:39.900
Bump that $59 million figure up to $90 million
and the outlook starts to seem a lot less

00:02:39.900 --> 00:02:40.480
rosy.

00:02:40.800 --> 00:02:45.040
They say there's no such thing as bad press,
but while the drummed up controversies surrounding

00:02:45.040 --> 00:02:49.340
First Man may not have hurt the film's box
office, they certainly haven't helped things

00:02:49.340 --> 00:02:49.840
either.

00:02:49.980 --> 00:02:53.060
So what are internet trolls pretending to
be upset about this time?

00:02:53.340 --> 00:02:57.220
Well, because the finished cut doesn't highlight
the planting of the American flag in the moon

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:01.120
landing scene, some people felt First Man
wasn't nationalistic enough.

00:03:01.200 --> 00:03:06.460
And needless to say, those same people weren't
too pleased when star Claire Foy used a Washington

00:03:06.470 --> 00:03:11.270
Monument metaphor to suggest that President
Donald Trump is, quote, "the giant penis of

00:03:11.270 --> 00:03:11.960
America."

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:13.760
"you're a bunch of boys!

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:15.610
Making models out of balsa wood.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:17.520
You don’t have anything under control."

00:03:18.220 --> 00:03:23.099
Even though First Man has had a disappointing
debut, there's still hope that it will eventually

00:03:23.099 --> 00:03:25.290
turn a profit — or even become a hit.

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:27.380
That's because we've literally seen this before.

00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:32.980
In 1983, The Right Stuff, which was also about
America's space program, debuted to poor box

00:03:32.980 --> 00:03:37.470
office figures and limped along in theaters
for weeks… until it earned eight Academy

00:03:37.470 --> 00:03:42.280
Award nominations, generating huge buzz and
leading to a commercial resurgence.

00:03:42.280 --> 00:03:46.580
Despite being released in October, The Right
Stuff's biggest box office weekend was at

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:50.380
the end of February following a huge re-release
prior to the Oscars.

00:03:50.490 --> 00:03:54.900
With Academy Award buzz already building around
Gosling and Foy, it looks like Universal's

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:59.740
best hope is to play the long game and hope
First Man catches fire on re-entry.

